Even though he's so close to Marshall, like I also, you know, I've observed about Ted observed about Ted in this first season, he is obsessed with plans, he's obsessed with order, he's obsessed with things going the way he wants, except when Robin comes in the picture, he'll rip up the plan, he'll rip up the party list, he'll do whatever, he'll improvise when Robin comes around.
尽管他和马歇尔那么要好，但我还……你知道的，我观察过泰德，在第一季里观察过泰德，他痴迷于计划，他痴迷于秩序，他痴迷于事情按照他想要的方式发展，除了罗宾出现的时候——只要罗宾出现，他就会撕毁计划，撕毁派对名单，随心所欲，随机应变。

00:08:37.102 --> 00:08:43.304
But also, he's got this perfect gate lined up, like the perfect ordered like from his imagination.
但同时，他心里也勾勒出了一幅完美的宏伟蓝图，就像是从他想象中走出来的那样井井有条。

00:08:43.304 --> 00:08:49.570
Weirdly, it's literally exactly what he's looking for and Lily calls any leaves and he goes to her.
奇怪的是，这简直完全就是他在寻找的东西，而莉莉一打电话他就离开，然后去找她。

00:08:49.570 --> 00:09:13.600
So it feels like, yeah, Robin is the tantalizing object of his romance, but Lily in distress, or any of his friends in distress, are also enough to have him rip up the schedule and go to them, which I think is more evidence of when people ask me what they love about Ted, what I love about Ted, I often say his loyalty.
所以感觉就像，是的，罗宾是他浪漫情调中诱人的目标，但陷入绝望的莉莉，或者陷入绝望的任何朋友，也同样能让他撕毁日程表去找他们，我认为这进一步证明了，当人们问我他们最喜欢泰德什么、我最喜欢泰德什么时，我经常会说是他的忠诚。

00:09:13.600 --> 00:09:14.919
What a good friend he is.
他真的是个好朋友。

00:09:14.919 --> 00:09:46.913
you know he's such a good friend he's such a good friend and I love how you played that scene because Ted is the way I took it and tell me if this is how it felt acting it I took it that Ted was there for Lily because they are best friends but also I saw it in Ted's eyes your eyes and playing the scene that Ted knew he had to live with the heaviness of this knowledge that he couldn't share with his other best friend Marshall and I felt like I felt Ted torn between being there on the the side of that road in Westchester or Dutchess County, where he is, and thinking about Marshall back home.
你知道的，他真的是个极好的朋友，我太喜欢你演那场戏的方式了，因为在我看来——泰德去是因为他们是最好的朋友，你告诉我你当时演的时候是不是这种感觉——我是觉得泰德陪着莉莉是因为他们是挚友，但我也从泰德的眼睛里、从你的眼神和表演中看出，泰德知道他必须背负这个沉重的秘密，而这个秘密他又不能分享给他的另一个挚友马歇尔。我能感觉到泰德内心备受煎熬，一边要在韦斯特切斯特或达奇斯县那条路边陪着她，一边又在想着家里的马歇尔。

00:09:46.913 --> 00:09:59.742
And the moment where he calls, where he has to actually talk on the phone briefly to Marshall, the guilt that he's talking to Marshall while he holds this terrible knowledge that Lilly is in this freakout that Marshall knows nothing about.
而在那个他给马歇尔打电话、必须跟马歇尔简短通电话的时刻，他一边怀着莉莉情绪崩溃而马歇尔一无所知的可怕秘密，一边跟马歇尔说话，那种内疚感……

00:09:59.742 --> 00:10:01.460
I thought you played that great.
我觉得你演得太棒了。

00:10:01.460 --> 00:10:05.218
There's like this real conflict, like conflicted energy to that scene.
那场戏里有一种真正的冲突感，充满了矛盾的情绪。

00:10:05.218 --> 00:10:06.667
Is that how it felt to you?
你当时是这种感觉吗？

00:10:06.667 --> 00:10:18.370
Like you were, you were trying to be the best friend to two people that the two missions didn't overlap I mean, for an actor, that's like a real gift, because it's like you wanna be pulled in three separate directions.
就像你在努力对两个人做好朋友，而这两个任务根本无法重合。我的意思是，对演员来说这简直是个天赋异禀的挑战，因为就像是你被三个不同的方向同时拉扯。

00:10:18.370 --> 00:10:24.610
Like you want to feel that stress and strain of, and it's also true.
就像你想去感受那种压力和紧绷感，而且这也很真实。

00:10:24.610 --> 00:10:34.850
I mean, I think we've all had experiences where you're in a group of friends or a trio or something and it's like the side group chat, right?
我的意思是，我想我们都有过这样的经历：当你身处一个朋友圈或三人小团体中时，就像是有一个私下的群聊，对吧？

00:10:34.850 --> 00:10:45.154
Like suddenly there's information being exchanged that is not meant for the group at large, and then you have to hold that, you know.
就像突然间开始交流一些并不打算让整个团体知道的信息，然后你必须保守这个秘密，你知道的。

00:10:45.154 --> 00:10:53.754
It's not quite, you know, someone's having an affair, but it is, it does feel like an infidelity to their plan.
这不太像是……你知道的，有人出轨了，但它确实感觉像是对他们原本计划的一种背叛。

00:10:53.754 --> 00:11:31.950
You know, he's, she's really thrust this thing in Ted's lap, and you know what I thought was funny was when she said it might have a flat tire, and then Ted pulled up and and Jordana leaners she goes Ted can't change a flat tire but he's an architect so I feel like he has the brain to change but then he does but then he does the greatest acting that I probably did in the episode was acting as if I just changed a flat tire The kind of like, oh, okay, oh, there you go, mission accomplished.
你知道的，她真的把这摊子事扔到了泰德怀里，而且你知道我觉得搞笑的是什么吗，当她说可能车胎瘪了的时候，然后泰德把车开过去，乔安娜·莱纳就说泰德不会换备胎，但他是个建筑师，所以我觉得他有换备胎的头脑，但随后他确实……但随后他展现了我在这集里可能做过的最棒的演技，那就是假装我刚刚换好了一个备胎，那种“哦，好吧，哦，行了，任务完成”的感觉。

00:11:31.950 --> 00:11:43.250
And I wrote you this little day to send you in New York City.
我给你写了这个小约会，让你去纽约市散散心。

00:11:43.250 --> 00:11:53.500
We'll be right back.
我们马上回来。

00:11:53.500 --> 00:11:55.629
And now, back to the show.
现在，回到节目中。

00:11:55.629 --> 00:11:58.149
Some people have just weird pockets of talent.
有些人就是有一些奇怪的特殊才能。

00:11:58.149 --> 00:12:03.509
Like in two truths and a lie Ted would like throw in, can change a tire and people be like, that's a lie.
就像在“两真一假”的游戏里，泰德可能会随口说“会换轮胎”，然后大家就会觉得“那是假的”。

00:12:03.509 --> 00:12:05.309
He's like, ah, no, it's a truth.
他就说：“啊，不，这是真的。”

00:12:05.309 --> 00:12:06.149
I can.
“我会的。”

00:12:06.149 --> 00:12:07.309
I'm from Cleveland.
“我是克利夫兰人。”

00:12:07.309 --> 00:12:08.710
That was a great scene.
那真是一场精彩的戏。

00:12:08.710 --> 00:12:14.990
I also love how early in the scene, Alison slash Lily starts tearing up, right?
我也很喜欢戏里刚开始的时候，艾莉森也就是莉莉开始眼眶湿润，对吧？

00:12:14.990 --> 00:12:19.429
When she's almost starting to cry as she's saying, like, no, no, no, I just want to see if I can get this thing.
当她边说边快要哭出来的时候，就像是“不，不，不，我只是想看看我能不能拿到这东西”。

00:12:19.429 --> 00:12:20.389
And then I'm going to let it go.
“然后我就把它放下。”

00:12:20.389 --> 00:12:23.590
And I feel like she's crying because she knows she's lying.
我觉得她在哭，因为她知道自己在撒谎。

00:12:23.590 --> 00:12:29.350
I love how she played that because she knows, she knows it's bigger than she just wanted to know if she could get it.
我很喜欢她的这种表演，因为她心里清楚，她很清楚这不仅仅是“她只是想知道自己能不能拿到”那么简单。

00:12:29.350 --> 00:12:30.870
If she gets it, she's gone.
如果她拿到了，她就一走了之了。

00:12:30.870 --> 00:12:39.110
She's going and she's pretending And if that's not true, and it's coming out of her eyes, that trying to hold that lie is coming out of her eyes.
她要走了，而且她还在假装。如果这并非出自真心，而泪水却从眼眶夺眶而出，那努力掩饰谎言的痛苦就化作了夺眶而出的泪水。

00:12:39.110 --> 00:12:42.509
And I thought that was really excellent acting on her part.
我觉得她这部分的演技真的非常出色。

00:12:42.509 --> 00:12:54.629
You know, once or twice a season, you guys really gave Allie like these kind of scenes where she would have like an aria or she would be like that, you know, that great rooftop scene with me and her later.
你知道的，一季里总有一两次，你们真的会给艾莉这类戏份，让她有一段独白，或者像后来她和我一起演的那场精彩的天台戏。

00:12:55.789 --> 00:13:00.789
She just consistently is just extraordinary in these scenes.
在这些戏里，她的表现一直都是无与伦比的出色。

00:13:01.350 --> 00:13:02.190
She's so good.
她太棒了。

00:13:02.190 --> 00:13:19.350
I think because Ali is so kind of known for more like comedic things or quirky things like you forget like she's an A plus dramatic actress like she's so can break your heart.
我想可能是因为艾莉以往多以喜剧或古怪的角色为人熟知，所以你会忘了她其实是个顶级的戏剧女演员——她真的很擅长让人心碎。

00:13:19.350 --> 00:13:22.149
And I don't know the way she delivered that mistakes thing.
而且我不知道她台词里讲到“犯错”那段是怎么表达出来的。

00:13:22.149 --> 00:13:39.610
I was almost like I was really like just as an actor I was like that slaloming down that hill and clearing all those flags like when you're like, that's a real high level of difficulty what she did because it's a really hard speech in terms of just the logic of it.
我当时就真的像是个演员在看别人顺着山坡疯狂回转、避开所有旗杆一样，你会觉得：她做到的难度系数真的很高，因为仅从台词逻辑来看，这是一段非常难的独白。

00:13:39.610 --> 00:13:45.529
And she's going too fast for Ted, but she herself had to understand it to memorize it, right?
而且她的语速比泰德还快，但她自己必须先理解才能背下来，对吧？

00:13:45.529 --> 00:13:54.377
So I just thought she did an incredible job throughout that thing, you know, being being both like manic, but also having like deep clarity through it in her mania.
所以我只是觉得她在整段戏里表现得不可思议，你知道的，既表现得有点狂躁，又在狂躁中展现出无比清醒的认知。

00:13:54.377 --> 00:13:57.183
It was really, it was a high level, a high wire act.
这真的是一个高难度的高空走钢丝表演。

00:13:57.183 --> 00:14:02.200
There's like a deep self-knowledge there to say, essentially, damn it, I've made no mistakes.
里面有一种深刻的自我认知，基本上就是在大喊：“该死，我从没犯过错。”

00:14:02.200 --> 00:14:05.923
This is the part where I get to at least flirt with making a big one.
“这是我至少能去跟犯个大错调情一下的部分。”

00:14:05.923 --> 00:14:07.757
And then I'm not going to make it.
“然后我不会真的去犯它。”

00:14:07.757 --> 00:14:11.911
I'll see if I can make it and then I'm going to let go of it and not make it.
“我看看自己能不能做到，然后我就把它放下，不去做这件事。”

00:14:11.911 --> 00:14:14.070
And she knows she's lying there herself.
而她自己心里也清楚她在撒谎。

00:14:14.070 --> 00:14:15.990
And she actually does have a point.
而且她其实也说得有道理。

00:14:15.990 --> 00:14:22.629
I think people, the people who in their family or and their friend group are the person that kind of holds shit together.
我觉得人们……那些在家庭或朋友圈里承担着把乱摊子收拾起来的角色。

00:14:22.629 --> 00:14:33.309
They're the cement, they're the load bearing support of the building, the building's gonna come down if you take away that piece, that wall, that column.
他们是水泥，他们是建筑物的承重支撑，如果你把那块砖、那面墙、那根柱子抽掉，建筑就会坍塌。

00:14:33.309 --> 00:14:40.070
That's Lily, and I think she has been living under that pressure for her entire life.
那就是莉莉，我觉得她一生都在这种压力下生活。

00:14:41.149 --> 00:14:51.750
I say this because some of this overlaps with my wife who was very much that and her family and friends and her family, with me and the kids, She's, some of this comes from her.
我这么说是因为这其中有些部分跟我妻子很像，她在她的家庭、朋友以及我们和孩子们的家庭里，非常扮演着这样的角色。

00:14:51.750 --> 00:14:53.629
Some of these last couple of episodes of the season come from her.
有些情节就源自于她。

00:14:53.750 --> 00:14:57.149
I will say that there were moments where she was like, that's really close.
本季最后这几集里的某些部分就取材于她。

00:14:57.149 --> 00:15:03.350
You really didn't give me a heads up that the dialogue was going to be exactly stuff that I kind of wrestle with in my life, which was a lesson.
我得说，有时候她会觉得：“这也太像了吧。”“你事先也没提醒我，这些台词居然全都是我在生活中苦苦挣扎的那些事儿。”这可真是个教训。

00:15:03.350 --> 00:15:15.950
Young Craig writer, young writer, Craig had to learn and really didn't and really just kept doing that, doing it the wrong way and like it would just air and people would go, oh, but I think that Alison plays that so well.
年轻的编剧克雷格，年轻的编剧克雷格不得不吸取教训，结果一开始没做好，还一直在用错误的方式继续写，直到它播出后大家纷纷感叹：“哦……”但我认为艾莉森把这个角色演得太好了。

00:15:15.950 --> 00:15:22.100
because she's, I think Alison, she shares some of that in her energy in the world, I think, right?
因为我觉得，艾莉森在面对世界时的某种能量里，也带有这种特质，对吧？

00:15:22.100 --> 00:15:23.254
And she shares on screen.
而且她在银幕上也展现了这一点。

00:15:23.254 --> 00:15:24.501
That's how she feels to us.
这就是她给我们留下的感觉。

00:15:24.501 --> 00:15:26.580
That's how that's her presence, her presence.
这就是她的存在感，她的气场。

00:15:26.580 --> 00:15:28.270
She was also in the cast.
她在剧组里也是这样。

00:15:28.270 --> 00:15:42.337
She was kind of the mama bear in terms of, I mean, Ali was definitely like, if I needed a doctor, or like, she just had a lot of answers to things of like, where you go when you need this, like, she's a mama.
她在某种程度上就像是个“老母亲”，我的意思是，艾莉绝对是那种——如果我需要找医生，或者诸如此类的事，她对各种事情都有很多门路，知道你需要的时候该去哪里找，她就像个妈妈。

00:15:42.337 --> 00:15:43.216
She's a mama.
她就像个妈妈。

00:15:43.216 --> 00:15:52.008
And I think that when you're the kind of hero child or the, you know, it's revealed later, like she had a very unstable childhood.
而且我认为，当你成为那种“被寄予厚望的孩子”，或者……你知道的，后来剧情揭晓了，她有一个非常动荡的童年。

00:15:52.008 --> 00:15:55.796
Her father is this kind of not ball board game inventor.
她的父亲是个有点不靠谱的棋盘游戏发明家。

00:15:55.796 --> 00:16:01.950
And, you know, she had to become an adult because she had children for parents essentially.
而且，你知道的，她不得不早早成熟，因为本质上她的父母才是需要被照顾的孩子。

00:16:01.950 --> 00:16:09.051
And I think when you get those people in either duress or in therapy, there's a lot of dissembling to do.
我想，当你让这样的人处于压力之下或者去做心理治疗时，会有很多伪装需要卸下。

00:16:09.051 --> 00:16:19.940
There's a lot of falling apart that has to happen because they have not been able to do that or allow, they feel like the whole structure will fall if they fall.
会有很多崩溃是必须要经历的，因为他们以前一直无法做到这一点，或者不允许自己这么做，他们觉得如果自己倒下了，整个结构就会分崩离析。

00:16:19.940 --> 00:16:30.289
So it can be an enormous relief to have them do that, but also to them, it's like they're letting down not just themselves, but their whole world, they're holding up.
所以让她们宣泄出来可能会是一种巨大的解脱，但对她们来说，这就像是不仅辜负了自己，还辜负了她们苦苦支撑的整个世界。

00:16:30.289 --> 00:16:39.809
And when you see that person and the audience sees Alice in that way, sees Lily that way, I think on the character see Lily that way, the audience sees Alice in that way.
当你看到这样一个人，当观众以这种方式看到艾莉森、看到莉莉时，我认为角色眼中的莉莉是这样的，观众眼中的艾莉森也是这样的。

00:16:39.809 --> 00:16:56.610
When you see that person who's that sturdy, who's that necessary to keep the world, to keep the planet spinning and keep gravity working and people from flying off into outer space, when that person breaks, it's fucking, it's potent to go back to that word potent.
当你看到那个如此坚强、为了维持世界运转、维持星球旋转、维持重力存在、防止人们飞向外太空而必不可少的人崩溃时，那种感觉真他妈的……回到刚才那个词，很有感染力。

00:16:56.610 --> 00:17:05.329
It's very potent when that person breaks, when that person cries, when that person has the breakdown in real life or as a character, it's very powerful.
当这样一个人崩溃、当这个人哭泣、当这个人在现实生活或作为角色发生精神崩溃时，那种冲击力非常强大。

00:17:05.329 --> 00:17:08.769
It's almost unsettling to watch it, right?
看着这一幕甚至会让人感到有些不安，对吧？

00:17:08.769 --> 00:17:14.837
unsettling to watch Alison slash Lily with this energy in this episode, unsettling in the best possible way.
看着艾莉森饰演的莉莉在本集中流露出这种情绪让人感到不安，但这是以最好的方式感到了不安。

00:17:14.837 --> 00:17:24.049
I mean, like, and it's what makes this episode work and what makes what makes it special and some of the best acting in season one, I think, is that P dot sequence.
我的意思是，这正是让这一集奏效的原因，也是让它变得特别、成为第一季中最佳表演之一的原因，我认为就是那段P点序列。

00:17:24.049 --> 00:17:34.671
And I also think the relative kind of swiftness of it, which is so startling to Marshall a little less to Ted just because he has more forewarning.
而且我也觉得这种情绪爆发的相对迅速，让马歇尔感到十分震惊，对泰德来说则没那么惊讶，因为他有更多的心理准备。

00:17:34.671 --> 00:17:51.940
But like, the swiftness of it feels right because it's the simmering underneath, it's the, there is a snap, there's a kind of thing of like, I need to, I think she's looking at this road ahead and she's seeing all these other doors closed.
但这种迅速感让人觉得很真实，因为它一直在暗中酝酿，有一个突然爆发的临界点，就像是……我觉得她看着前方的道路，发现所有其他的门都关上了。

00:17:51.940 --> 00:17:52.980
We've talked a lot about this.
我们讨论过很多次这个。

00:17:52.980 --> 00:17:56.900
Like a lot about how I met mother, especially season one is about options.
比如《老爸老妈浪漫史》尤其是第一季，很大程度上是关于选择的。

00:17:56.900 --> 00:18:00.259
You know, we have a lot of options, which roads are we gonna take?
你知道的，我们有很多选择，我们究竟该走哪条路？

00:18:00.259 --> 00:18:02.900
And she literally like takes off on a road.
而她字面意义上地踏上了一条路。

00:18:02.900 --> 00:18:06.940
She goes, she takes this car and goes, goes away.
她开着这辆车，头也不回地走了。

00:18:06.940 --> 00:18:09.859
No one ever said Carter and I were subtle with metaphors.
从来没人说过卡特和我玩隐喻时会很委婉。

00:18:09.859 --> 00:18:11.940
It's an actual road.
这真的是一条路。

