00:42:39.119 --> 00:42:50.268
Ted is actually tuning into some universal vibration here in this episode because he goes there to help Lilly, that falls apart, Robbins there to help him.
泰德在这一集里其实是接上某种宇宙的共振了，因为他去那是为了帮莉莉，结果搞砸了，罗宾在那儿帮他。

00:42:50.268 --> 00:42:53.001
Everything's there in his life, right?
他生活中的一切都在那儿，对吧？

00:42:53.001 --> 00:42:54.080
It's all there.
全都在那儿。

00:42:54.080 --> 00:42:55.662
It's a closed circuit.
这是一个闭环。

00:42:55.662 --> 00:42:56.454
It's there.
它就在那儿。

00:42:56.454 --> 00:43:00.841
His life has what he needs in this episode and he knows that.
在这集中，他的生活拥有了他所需要的一切，而他深知这一点。

00:43:00.841 --> 00:43:09.832
Well, I wonder, and I'm sure that on some level, this is true, but if Lillian Marshall can maybe not make it and get rattled.
嗯，我在想——而且我确信在某种程度上确实如此——莉莉和马修也许会挺不过去并阵脚大乱。

00:43:09.832 --> 00:43:11.198
Nothing is certain.
没有什么什么是确定的。

00:43:11.198 --> 00:43:12.493
There is no order.
没有什么秩序可言。

00:43:12.493 --> 00:43:15.442
There is nothing we can really depend on.
没有什么我们可以真正依赖。

00:43:15.442 --> 00:43:19.686
You might as well follow your heart and see where it leads.
你不如顺从你的内心，看看它会把你带向何方。

00:43:19.686 --> 00:43:26.590
And I love that last conversation about milk to bring us back to the maybe perhaps missed title.
我喜欢最后关于牛奶的那段对话，把我们拉回了那个也许被忽略了的剧集标题。

00:43:26.590 --> 00:43:31.410
But Lillian Tedder actually having a telepathic conversation there.
但莉莉和泰德其实在那里进行了一场心灵感应般的对话。

00:43:31.409 --> 00:43:36.550
They're just having a different conversation for Marshall.
他们只是在和马修进行一场不同的对话。

00:43:36.550 --> 00:43:40.070
I think Ted is seeing the imperfection of the perfect couple.
我觉得泰德看到了完美情侣的不完美之处。

00:43:40.070 --> 00:43:41.389
It's the perfect couple.
这就是那对完美情侣。

00:43:41.389 --> 00:43:55.670
He's been trying to replicate this perfect couple and he's seeing that there is imperfection in this perfect couple and his best friend Marshall doesn't know that his other best friend Lily is experiencing something very unsettling and I think that's right.
他一直在试图复制这对完美情侣，而他现在看到这对完美情侣其实也有不完美的地方，他的好朋友马修并不知道他的另一个好朋友莉莉正在经历一些非常让人心神不宁的事情，我觉得这很对。

00:43:55.670 --> 00:44:01.630
I think that gives Ted free rein to go chase what could be imperfect for him.
我觉得这给了泰德全权去追求对他来说可能并不完美的事物。

00:44:01.630 --> 00:44:04.150
but it's what he wants and it's what he needs to see through.
但那是他想要的，也是他需要亲历的。

00:44:04.150 --> 00:44:06.389
And that's our season finale.
这就是我们的季终集。

00:44:06.389 --> 00:44:07.590
Very next episode.
紧接着下一集。

00:44:07.590 --> 00:44:11.550
We're almost at the end of season one of both the TV show and the podcast.
无论是这部电视剧还是这个播客，我们都快要迎来第一季的尾声了。

00:44:11.550 --> 00:44:14.070
You really teed up a finale really beautifully here.
你真的把季终集铺垫得非常精彩。

00:44:14.070 --> 00:44:23.789
So it definitely makes me want to tune in and watch the finale and we'll be discussing it next week and I'm really looking forward to it.
这绝对让我很想收看大结局，我们下周会讨论它，我真的很期待。

00:44:23.789 --> 00:44:32.800
Well, we've come to the end of the show and we like to end this show and every show with a letter that we've received.
好了，节目接近尾声了，我们习惯用一封收到的来信来结束本期以及每一期节目。

00:44:32.800 --> 00:44:49.524
If you would like to write us a letter or record a voice note about what how I met your mother means to you or what your relationship has been to the show, please go to how we made your mother dot com h w m y m dot com.
如果你想给我们写信，或者录一段语音留言，聊聊《老爸老妈浪漫史》对你意味着什么，或者你与这部剧有什么样的羁绊，请访问 how we made your mother 点 com，即 hwmym 点 com。

00:44:49.524 --> 00:44:54.946
Go to contact and follow the instructions there should be pretty clear.
点击联系我们，按照上面的说明操作，应该非常清楚。

00:44:54.946 --> 00:45:06.782
But we've just gotten flooded with beautiful reflections and people letting us know how this show came to them and how it's changed them and affected them.
不过我们已经收到了大量美好的感悟，大家纷纷告诉我们这部剧是如何走入他们的生活，又是如何改变和影响他们的。

00:45:06.782 --> 00:45:10.219
And we have a beautiful letter to read today.
今天我们有一封非常美妙的信要读。

00:45:10.219 --> 00:45:12.510
This is from Howard in Taiwan.
这是来自台湾的霍华德（Howard）写的。

00:45:13.769 --> 00:45:17.651
I want to tell you a story about my soulmate, the one true love of my life.
我想给你们讲一个关于我的灵魂伴侣、我生命中唯一的真爱的故事。

00:45:17.651 --> 00:45:21.533
The first time I met my girlfriend was during our freshman year of college.
我和女友第一次见面是在我们大学一年级的时候。

00:45:21.533 --> 00:45:27.329
She had already watched how I met your mother multiple times, but she was the one who introduced me to the show.
她当时已经看过好几遍《老爸老妈浪漫史》了，但正是她把我带入了这部剧。

00:45:27.329 --> 00:45:32.194
We shared many of the same thoughts about himium which helped us build a wonderful connection.
我们对这部剧有着许多相同的看法，这帮我们建立了一种奇妙的连接。

00:45:32.194 --> 00:45:37.110
Thank God we were like Lily and Marshall to people who found true love from the very beginning.
谢天谢地，我们就像从一开始就找到真爱的人心中的莉莉和马修一样。

00:45:37.110 --> 00:45:40.837
By the end of this year we will be celebrating our six-year anniversary.
今年年底我们将庆祝我们在一起六周年的纪念日。

00:45:40.837 --> 00:45:43.579
Now I'm about to pursue my master's degree in the US.
现在我即将去美国攻读硕士学位。

00:45:44.300 --> 00:45:52.051
Sometimes I feel like it's a mistake because I'm deeply in love with my girlfriend, my country, Taiwan, and every single friend I have there.
有时我觉得这是一个错误，因为我深深地爱着我的女友、我的祖国台湾，以及我在那里遇到的每一个朋友。

00:45:52.051 --> 00:45:55.899
Studying abroad could easily weaken or even break those relationships.
出国留学很可能会削弱甚至切断这些关系。

00:45:55.899 --> 00:46:00.517
However, I still need to go ahead to find out if this path is truly worth it for me.
然而，我还是得勇往直前，去看看这条路对我来说是否真的值得。

00:46:00.517 --> 00:46:07.993
This situation reminds me of Lily in episode 21, when she wanted to find out if she was meant to pursue her dream of becoming an artist.
这种情况让我想起了第21集里的莉莉，当时她想弄清楚自己是否应该去追求成为艺术家的梦想。

00:46:07.993 --> 00:46:22.561
In that episode, she stood in the middle of nowhere and told Ted, I know it's a mistake, but there are certain things in life where you know it's a mistake, but you don't really know it's a mistake because the only way to know it's a mistake is to make the mistake.
在那一集里，她站在荒郊野岭对泰德说：我知道这是一个错误，但生活中有某些事情，你知道这是一个错误，但你其实并不真正知道它是错误，因为知道它是错误的唯一方法就是犯下这个错误。

00:46:22.561 --> 00:46:25.860
And then you look back and and say, yep, that was a mistake.
然后你回过头来说，没错，那确实是个错误。

00:46:25.860 --> 00:46:35.570
So really, the bigger mistake would be to not make the mistake, because then you'd go your whole life not really knowing if something is a mistake or not.
所以实际上，更大的错误是不去犯这个错误，因为那样你就会一辈子都不知道某件事到底是不是错误。

00:46:35.570 --> 00:46:40.889
Thank you again to this show for giving me the courage to pursue my dreams and to my girl.
再次感谢这部剧给了我追求梦想的勇气，也谢谢我的女孩。

00:46:40.889 --> 00:46:45.690
By the time you reach this episode, I will probably be in a graduate program in the US.
当你们听到这一集的时候，我可能已经在美国的某个研究生项目里了。

00:46:45.690 --> 00:46:48.650
So I want to tell you, don't be afraid.
所以我想对你说，不要害怕。

00:46:48.650 --> 00:46:50.409
We can make it through this.
我们一定能熬过去的。

00:46:50.409 --> 00:46:51.849
Wait for me.
等我。

00:46:51.849 --> 00:46:54.550
Love you, my dear Anna, Howard.
爱你的，我亲爱的安娜，霍华德。

00:46:56.130 --> 00:46:56.969
Wow.
哇。

00:46:58.329 --> 00:46:59.170
Jordana's crying.
若妲娜哭了。

00:46:59.170 --> 00:47:05.369
Usually the beginnings of the episodes makes me, I hear it, Jordana, Josh's life, Jordana, is crying in the background from that letter.
通常节目的开头会让我……我听到背景里若妲娜在因为那封信而哭泣。

00:47:05.369 --> 00:47:07.940
That letter's unbelievable.
那封信太不可思议了。

00:47:07.940 --> 00:47:11.239
Oh my God, that got her, that got me too.
哦天哪，感动了她，也感动了我。

00:47:11.239 --> 00:47:13.340
Wow, thank you for sharing that, Howard.
哇，谢谢你分享这个，霍华德。

00:47:14.889 --> 00:47:23.050
Beautiful, that's a beautiful, oh my God, I so hope that she hears this, that this is a surprise to her that she hears this.
太美好了，这是一封美好的信，天哪，我太希望她能听到这个，希望这对她来说是个惊喜。

00:47:23.050 --> 00:47:28.329
If Anna's not, if Anna's not in the business of listening to the C block, you gotta remind her.
如果安娜平时不听C段的内容，你得提醒她一下。

00:47:28.329 --> 00:47:29.849
Stay tuned to the end.
收听到最后。

00:47:29.849 --> 00:47:32.690
Sits through the pretty letter ad.
听完那些动听的信件广告。

00:47:32.690 --> 00:47:34.570
There's something really beautiful after it.
那之后会有非常美妙的事情。

00:47:34.570 --> 00:47:38.769
We're gonna talk about cats peeing, and then you're gonna hear undying devotion from Howard.
我们接下来要聊聊猫咪小便的事，然后你们会听到霍华德永恒的深情。

00:47:39.650 --> 00:47:41.010
That was so beautiful.
那真的太美好了。

00:47:41.010 --> 00:47:42.530
I wish you guys the best of luck.
我祝你们好运。

00:47:42.530 --> 00:47:46.050
I'm so glad the show speaks to you in that way.
我很高兴这部剧能以这种方式触动你们。

00:47:46.050 --> 00:47:50.929
Oh boy, I think going to take that adventure is an amazing thing to do.
天哪，我觉得去开启那场冒险是一件了不起的事。

00:47:50.929 --> 00:47:56.929
And I think you sound very in love and have a good feeling it's gonna go well like it did.
而且我觉得听得出你深陷爱河，我也有一种强烈的直觉，一切都会像当年那样顺利。

00:47:56.929 --> 00:48:01.969
In the end, in the long run, there was some turbulence from Marshall and Lily, but spoilers, they were okay.
最终，从长远来看，马歇尔和莉莉之间虽然有过一些波折，但剧透一下，他们最后很好。

00:48:01.969 --> 00:48:10.130
I gotta say, Craig, I enjoyed reading that speech from Lily a little slower than she delivers it.
我得说，克雷格，我很喜欢听你用比莉莉本人更慢的语速来朗读那段演讲。

00:48:10.130 --> 00:48:12.010
There's a lot of wisdom in that speech.
那段演讲里蕴含着很多智慧。

00:48:12.010 --> 00:48:13.690
And there's a lot of- There's a lot of wisdom.
而且有很多——有很多智慧。

00:48:13.690 --> 00:48:14.530
She's manic.
她有点歇斯底里。

00:48:14.530 --> 00:48:30.110
But she's also in some ways articulating core theme or philosophy of how we met your mother is like, you can plot everything out, but you've got to live it forward and you've got to step in the potholes and twist your ankle, you know, to learn and where you're going.
但她在某种程度上也阐明了《老爸老妈浪漫史》的核心主题或哲学，那就是：你可以把一切都计划好，但你必须向前生活，你必须踏入水坑、扭伤脚踝，你知道的，这样才能学会成长并找到前行的方向。

00:48:30.110 --> 00:48:35.469
As you read it, which I enjoyed hearing you read that speech in a different tone and sort of it was like a good cover.
当你朗读它的时候，我很享受听你用不同的语调来朗读那段演讲，这就像是一次精彩的翻唱。

00:48:35.469 --> 00:48:40.309
It was like you took a rock song and slowed it down to a ballad there, one of those.
就像你把一首摇滚歌曲放慢成了一首民谣，其中一首那种风格的歌。

00:48:40.309 --> 00:48:45.150
And I thought of Jimmy Stewart and it's a wonderful life.
让我想到了吉姆·斯图尔特和《生活多美好》。

00:48:45.150 --> 00:48:52.909
That's what I was thinking of as you were reading that because there's this kind of yearning and like, I've got to go out into the world, I've got to do these things.
当你在读那段话时，我脑子里想的就是这个，因为里面有一种渴望，就像是“我必须去外面的世界，我必须去做这些事情”。

00:48:52.909 --> 00:48:56.150
But there's also this feeling of there's so much here for me.
但同时也有这样一种感觉：这里有太多属于我的东西。

00:48:56.150 --> 00:48:59.030
There's so much here for me.
这里有太多属于我的东西。

00:48:59.030 --> 00:49:00.750
And what a universal conundrum.
这是一个多么普遍的难题啊。

00:49:00.750 --> 00:49:05.630
Do I go out seeking everything outside or do I realize I have enough here?
我是该出去寻找外面的所有一切，还是意识到我在这里已经拥有足够多了？

00:49:05.630 --> 00:49:07.789
Sometimes you get to do both and it works out.
有时候你两者都能兼顾，而且结果很不错。

00:49:07.789 --> 00:49:09.469
And I hope that's what Howard gets to go do.
我希望霍华德也能这样。

00:49:09.469 --> 00:49:11.369
He gets to go see the world.
他去看看外面的世界。

00:49:11.369 --> 00:49:15.989
on his world is still there waiting for him and with him through that.
而他的世界依然在那里等着他，并一如既往地陪伴着他。

00:49:15.989 --> 00:49:26.369
And I think that to share that, to trust that person, to trust that your life and your world is going to be there on the other side is a huge and wonderful act of faith.
我觉得，能够去分享这一点，去信任那个人，去坚信你的生活和你的世界在经历这一切之后依然会在原地，这是一种巨大而美好的信念。

00:49:26.369 --> 00:49:39.820
And I think that if you lose something or if something is shaken or challenged by that, that can also in the long run be a good thing and lead to something stronger on the other side, even if it's a little different than you thought.
而且我认为，如果你因此失去了什么，或者有什么受到了动摇和挑战，从长远来看，这也可能是一件好事，并能在经历风雨后孕育出更坚固的东西，哪怕它和你想的有点不一样。

00:49:39.820 --> 00:49:41.019
So I just wish you the best of luck.
所以我只想祝你们好运。

00:49:41.019 --> 00:49:46.420
I think it's brave and exciting and lovely what you're doing Howard, so thank you for sharing that.
我觉得你做的事很勇敢、很激动人心也很可爱，霍华德，谢谢你分享这一切。

00:49:46.420 --> 00:49:55.960
I am guilty, please equip me, all sins are forgiven, in New York City.
我有罪，请宽恕我，在纽约市，所有的罪孽都被赦免。

